Subject: [PATCH] msm: mdss: retire fences are relative to the timeline

__vsync_retire_get_fence numbers a fence 1 + retire_cnt, but mdss_get_sync_fence
takes that as the timeline's absolute value. ASUS' 3.10 added the timeline's value.
In steady use this goes unnoticed: nearly every fence is number 1, signaled from
birth. After a frame fails the numbers go up and then down again, next_value goes
back with them, and mdss_inc_timeline only advances within next_value, so the
highest fence never signals, not even after turning the panel off. SurfaceFlinger
waits for it as the present fence and composes nothing more.

Number them from the timeline's value, so that they only grow. With the display
off, where the caller's fallback would take a number from the release timeline, use
a fence that goes with those pending, or one already reached if there are none.
---
--- drivers/video/fbdev/msm/mdss_mdp_overlay.c
+++ drivers/video/fbdev/msm/mdss_mdp_overlay.c
@@ -6380,6 +6380,7 @@
 	struct msm_fb_data_type *mfd;
 	struct mdss_overlay_private *mdp5_data;
 	struct mdss_mdp_ctl *ctl;
+	struct mdss_timeline *tl;
 	int value;
 
 	mfd = container_of(sync_pt_data, typeof(*mfd), mdp_sync_pt_data);
@@ -6392,16 +6393,20 @@
 	if (!ctl->ops.add_vsync_handler)
 		return ERR_PTR(-EOPNOTSUPP);
 
+	tl = mfd->mdp_sync_pt_data.timeline_retire;
+
 	if (!mdss_mdp_ctl_is_power_on(ctl)) {
+		/* No vsync will retire this one: it goes with those pending */
 		pr_debug("fb%d vsync pending first update\n", mfd->index);
-		return ERR_PTR(-EPERM);
-	}
-
-	value = 1 + mdp5_data->retire_cnt;
+		return mdss_fb_sync_get_fence(tl, "mdp-retire",
+				mdss_get_timeline_retire_ts(tl) +
+				mdp5_data->retire_cnt);
+	}
+
+	value = mdss_get_timeline_retire_ts(tl) + 1 + mdp5_data->retire_cnt;
 	mdp5_data->retire_cnt++;
 
-	return mdss_fb_sync_get_fence(mfd->mdp_sync_pt_data.timeline_retire,
-			"mdp-retire", value);
+	return mdss_fb_sync_get_fence(tl, "mdp-retire", value);
 }
 
 static int __vsync_set_vsync_handler(struct msm_fb_data_type *mfd)
